# Planning docs and local agent instructions. Kept out of the repo on
# purpose: they carry candid strategy and job-search framing. They are still
# the working knowledge base, just not version-controlled here.
#
# docs/* (not docs/) is deliberate: git cannot re-include a file inside a
# fully-excluded directory, so "docs/" here would silently defeat the
# negations below (this actually happened, caught 2026-09-01,
# DECISION_LOG.md was never tracked despite its negation line existing).
# docs/* excludes the directory's contents one level at a time, which
# negation can still see into.
docs/*
!docs/DECISION_LOG.md
# RESULTS.md is evidence for the Tier 1 README milestone, not private
# planning material like PROJECT_PLAN.md/CONCEPTS.md/START_HERE.md; tracked
# for the same reason DECISION_LOG.md is (2026-09-02).
!docs/RESULTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Corpus full text. Hundreds of MB of PMC OA JATS XML, regenerable from
# corpus/manifest.csv + corpus/run_info.json + ingestion/pull_corpus.py.
# manifest.csv carries a per-file sha256, so any re-fetch is byte-verifiable
# without the blobs living in git. corpus/manifest.csv and corpus/run_info.json
# are NOT ignored: they are the reproducibility record and must be committed.
corpus/xml/
ingestion/corpus/xml/

# eval/: held-out XML for negative cases moves here, not deleted. Regenerable
# the same way corpus/xml/ is. eval/held_out/held_out_pmcids.csv is NOT
# ignored: it's the record of which pmcids are held out and why.
eval/held_out/xml/
eval/coverage_candidates*.csv

# eval/runs/: baseline and scorer outputs (LLM-generated answers, score.py's
# --out JSON). Regenerated by every run, model-version- and prompt-version-
# dependent; the durable record of a run is its RESULTS.md row plus the
# .meta.json committed alongside it if that becomes worth keeping, not
# these files by default.
eval/runs/

# Kappa calibration worksheets: generated from a specific answers file
# (make_kappa_worksheet.py), and once filled in, contain one person's
# working hand-labels. Regenerable; the durable record of a calibration
# result is a DECISION_LOG.md / RESULTS.md entry, not this file.
eval/kappa_worksheet*.md

# eval/benchmarks/: downloaded benchmark datasets (SciFact, NFCorpus, etc.)
# are regenerable from download_datasets.py. Code (loader.py, test_loader.py)
# is committed; data files (.jsonl, .txt) are not.
eval/benchmarks/scifact/
eval/benchmarks/nfcorpus/

# Step 0c service: per-request logs and load-test summaries are regenerated
# by every run and would silently overwrite each other under git, the exact
# anti-pattern RESULTS.md's append-only rule exists to avoid. The durable
# record of a load test is the RESULTS.md row, not these files.
service/logs/
service/loadtest_result*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.env

# OS
.DS_Store
